17592186045417] [17592186179155 #edb/ref 1080 "24" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179155 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179155 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e8802437-9f26-5e47-b836-a50a564ead55" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179156 #edb/ref 1080 "6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179156 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179156 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0c1ec69d-8237-53ab-b125-deba7bb578fa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179157 #edb/ref 1080 "48" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179157 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179157 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "31e69d82-7c37-5b8c-a0a6-d027fcca6a8e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179521 #edb/ref 1069 "e-6117" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179521 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the following partitions:\n\n- $P_1 = \\left\\{x_0, x_1, \\ldots, x_m\\right\\}$ is a partition of the interval $[4, 6]$\n\n- $P_2 = \\left\\{y_0, y_1, \\ldots, y_n\\right\\}$ is a partition of the interval $[2, 6]$\n\nCalculate  $\\displaystyle\\sum_{i=1}^m\\sum_{j=1}^n (x_i + x_{i-1})\\Delta x_i \\Delta y_j,$ where $\\Delta x_i = x_i - x_{i-1}$ and $\\Delta y_j = y_j - y_{j-1}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179521 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "500e1ff1-1a58-57f5-8d85-32ff78dafb35" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179521 #edb/ref 1074 "Using the product rule, we can write the summation as\n\n$$\n\\sum_{i=1}^m (x_i + x_{i-1})\\Delta x_i \\cdot \\sum_{j=1}^n \\Delta y_j.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\displaystyle \\sum_{j=1}^n\\Delta y_j$ is just the length of the interval $[2, 6].$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}=6-2=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the sum over $i,$ we can evaluate it as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i} & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{0})Δ{x}_{1}+({x}_{2}+{x}_{1})Δ{x}_{2}+⋯+({x}_{m}+{x}_{m-1})Δ{x}_{m} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}\\,+\\,{x}_{0})({x}_{1}\\,-\\,{x}_{0})+({x}_{2}\\,+\\,{x}_{1})({x}_{2}\\,-\\,{x}_{1})+({x}_{m}\\,+\\,{x}_{m-1})({x}_{m}\\,-\\,{x}_{m-1}) \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2})+({x}_{2}^{2}-{x}_{1}^{2})+⋯+({x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{m-1}^{2}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{x}_{1}^{2}}-{x}_{0}^{2})+(\\cancel{{x}_{2}^{2}}-\\cancel{{x}_{1}^{2}})+⋯+({x}_{m}^{2}-\\cancel{{x}_{m-1}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-{x}_{0}^{2}+{x}_{m}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & ={6}^{2}-{4}^{2} \\\\  & =20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombining our results, we finally arrive at \n\n$$\n\\sum_{i=1}^m (x_i + x_{i-1})\\Delta x_i \\cdot \\sum_{j=1}^n\\Delta y_j = 20\\cdot 4 = 80.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179584 #edb/ref 1069 "e-9482" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179584 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the following partitions:\n\n- $P_1 = \\left\\{x_0, x_1, \\ldots, x_m\\right\\}$ is a partition of the interval $[-1, 2]$\n\n- $P_2 = \\left\\{y_0, y_1, \\ldots, y_n\\right\\}$ is a partition of the interval $[2, 3]$\n\nCalculate $\\displaystyle \\sum_{i=1}^m\\sum_{j=1}^n {3} \\Delta x_i \\Delta y_j,$ where $\\Delta x_i = x_i - x_{i-1}$ and $\\Delta y_j = y_j - y_{j-1}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179584 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e2f01953-2fb1-5ddb-83ae-5d8a73e7f7ac" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179584 #edb/ref 1074 "Using the constant multiple and product rules, we can write the summation as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}3Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} & =3{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\  & =3{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $\\displaystyle \\sum_{i=1}^m\\Delta x_i$ and $\\displaystyle \\sum_{j=1}^n\\Delta y_j$ are just the lengths of the intervals $[-1, 2]$ and $[2,3]$ respectively. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i} & =2-(-1)=3, \\\\ {\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j} & =3-2=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombining our results, we have\n\n$$\n3 \\sum_{i=1}^m \\Delta x_i \\sum_{j=1}^n \\Delta y_j = 3 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 1 = 9.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179666 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049943 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179666 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186180268 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179666 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186180269 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179666 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186256778 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179666 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186275217 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179666 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186275218 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179666 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186275219 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179666 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186275220 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179666 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186526001 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179666 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186526047 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179666 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186526049 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179666 #edb/ref 1039 "Computing a Double Sum Over a Rectangular Partition Using a Difference of Squares" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179666 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186179521 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179666 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "d5ee41f2-7116-52f4-b1f7-923997d994ab" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179722 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048800 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179722 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049629 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179722 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186179979 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179722 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186180267 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179722 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186256777 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179722 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186275216 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179722 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186339124 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179722 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186339125 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179722 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186525988 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179722 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186526042 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179722 #edb/ref 1039 "Computing a Double Sum Over a Rectangular Partition" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179722 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186179584 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179722 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "9f913fab-d0b5-5e9e-b292-039afe4a148c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179852 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186180380 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179852 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186180463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179852 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186180466 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179852 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186180472 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179852 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179852 #edb/ref 1045 "Calculating Double Summations Over Partitions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179852 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186180466 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179852 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049574 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179852 #edb/ref 1050 420.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179852 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "66d6f87f-f2db-557c-9687-6430c93f2f7b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179979 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186255963 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179979 #edb/ref 1069 "q-122867" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179979 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179979 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the following partitions:\n\n- ${P}_{1}=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\}$ is a partition of the interval $[0,2]$\n\n- ${P}_{2}=\\{{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}\\}$ is a partition of the interval $[1,6]$\n\nCalculate ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j},$ where $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179979 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7cb18f0a-5793-5799-850f-ef66cbf9de18" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186179979 #edb/ref 1074 "Using the product rule, we can write the summation as\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}.\n$$\n\nNote that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}$ and ${\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}$ are just the lengths of the intervals $[0,2]$ and $[1,6]$ respectively. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i} & =2-0=2, \\\\ {\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j} & =6-1=5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombining our results, we have\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}=2\\cdot 5=10.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180268 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186179152 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180268 #edb/ref 1069 "q-72129" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180268 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180268 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the following partitions:\n\n- ${P}_{1}=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\}$ is a partition of the interval $[2,5]$\n\n- ${P}_{2}=\\{{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}\\}$ is a partition of the interval $[0,2]$\n\nCalculate ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j}+{y}_{j-1})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j},$ where $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180268 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a88af1ba-c0a1-5207-b3ae-5df258155f41" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180268 #edb/ref 1074 "Using the product rule, we can write the summation as\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}\\cdot {\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j}+{y}_{j-1})Δ{y}_{j}.\n$$\n\nNote that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}$ is just the length of the interval $[2,5].$ So, we have\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}=5-2=3.\n$$\n\nFor the sum over $j,$ we evaluate it as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j}+{y}_{j-1})Δ{y}_{j} & =({y}_{1}+{y}_{0})Δ{y}_{1}+({y}_{2}+{y}_{1})Δ{y}_{2}+⋯+({y}_{n}+{x}_{n-1})Δ{y}_{n} \\\\  & =({y}_{1}+{y}_{0})({y}_{1}-{y}_{0})+({y}_{2}+{y}_{1})({y}_{2}-{y}_{1})+⋯+({y}_{n}+{x}_{n-1})({y}_{n}-{y}_{n-1}) \\\\  & =({y}_{1}^{2}-{y}_{0}^{2})+({y}_{2}^{2}-{y}_{1}^{2})+⋯+({y}_{n}^{2}-{y}_{n-1}^{2}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{y}_{1}^{2}}-{y}_{0}^{2})+(\\cancel{{y}_{2}^{2}}-\\cancel{{y}_{1}^{2}})+⋯+({y}_{n}^{2}-\\cancel{{y}_{n-1}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-{y}_{0}^{2}+{y}_{n}^{2} \\\\  & ={y}_{n}^{2}-{y}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & ={2}^{2}-{0}^{2} \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombining our results, we finally arrive at\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}\\cdot {\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j}+{y}_{j-1})Δ{y}_{j}=3\\cdot 4=12.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180380 #edb/ref 1061 22706 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180380 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "18a56983-3d17-54bb-bb04-5048fdc84982" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180380 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186179666 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180463 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186180380 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180463 #edb/ref 1061 35490 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180463 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "1358c412-56fe-52c5-a421-4ae462f72bc8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180463 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186179722 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180466 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186180472 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180466 #edb/ref 1061 35499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180466 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b0d06c7f-0e78-510d-8852-82dea5166908" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180466 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186180707 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180472 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186180463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180472 #edb/ref 1061 35548 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180472 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b2095dad-9a02-54e5-a167-0babe1804a2a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180472 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186180710 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180707 #edb/ref 1064 "Just as we can form partitions of closed intervals of the real line, we can also partition rectangular regions in the Cartesian plane.\n\nTo demonstrate, consider the rectangle ![](images/7f/7f4a14fac9a5f43bfd4ab81190cc4a53b04b829e342ea5681cf7e44bcddb2ea8.svg) shown below.\n\n![](images/b2/b2b9753f603902f8fc3b86c7bc58c927fca6e25c26b018ce85e665b47d75b77b.png)\n\nWe can describe the entire rectangle as ![](images/d6/d6e3d65ec5ef708e7d2f8368b43f0b05b2f0488b533a3ff6b46fd8297505894e.svg) where ![](images/66/66d58377d47e96b8baecdfbc2c2365f86825f2e43e17dfaac2225d1de20191c1.svg) denotes the Cartesian product.\n\nNow, let's partition ![](images/08/085f4d77675f3cb7323d94feaa9eaa38f2fecb26c0f8483895f9ddf36b8d319d.svg) into ![](images/37/37e17c4a2302e6352fb7186621c9c43bb5e99d43a8a0bc700c0181d36c6cc915.svg) rectangles of equal area, as shown below.\n\n![](images/10/10c85c7b9034a7cd342c5360a13eca471b103e769415a3459e7841c3d948ee7d.png)\n\nNote that we can describe our partition without a diagram as follows:\n\n- The partition of the ![](images/fc/fcc5df999e3b49fae1685ee0ab5bd03709804e1dd49f2ee722c4269eb0f5506d.svg)-interval ![](images/10/10afad0ff28bd2c5b5f3450dd6a83c4c6263cf628e8f405c7ff0d06ed7249072.svg) can be expressed as ![](images/bf/bf81cbc93793a83bbd68b3de440efd7329b8979e6ad9ca76a755938ba1079955.svg) where ![](images/67/674ac6553524f5663674850d81bea00ec8c59ee651fd2f4c942e0ab0a8a5d790.svg) ![](images/44/44fabdac948e1c3466dde55f202f25d1c267c85e22f0d38d8a1deed12ce2a929.svg) ![](images/5a/5ad873e1f6b4b1ba4a7810e18f8ab571d5bd3f8aaa4d72401c7bd19721a389e3.svg) and ![](images/f0/f0b8129f0d98db64a6be3240f33cf4b91e651fa2f2329d0258beba183624a977.svg)\n\n- The partition of the ![](images/1d/1d9b846cface9f9348e4081a0dd87dd254bf26663c12aa0d1a15aa24d2393261.svg)-interval ![](images/2e/2e43b93bdeca20a22541e4b289efb7e37f3b6a391bfed32323c4e3a3c7cda162.svg) can be expressed as ![](images/c3/c38a1873b3c68a6d204981670a7360f59512b1b42ce835b795b6be24619a2a6a.svg) where ![](images/a9/a92c357a02416f0914aa679bd177f1d72f7b52e2f063371fe36d8db0b2a0ead6.svg) ![](images/7a/7afd61dbfbaad2470afc104718dd99118e9f4cbfa82a63b4d0abb0b2563179c7.svg) and ![](images/4a/4a6fda6532f4b6963586cfbcb6c3d2174940834d2ed22645497d48f0788ba384.svg)\n\n- The partition of the entire rectangle can be described as ![](images/17/174f77031e6ccf34569f7b02648f9199b402a08898161efc74bff691c34faf5b.svg)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180707 #edb/ref 1065 5780 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180707 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "e8975bb9-0b71-53a4-98ad-d358801bde48" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180707 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180710 #edb/ref 1064 "We have our partition $P = P_1\\times P_2,$ shown below.\n\n![](images/0e/0e497b6d43e4d46d4fad71bc2b81810c972b0e306817d161ad3a2e285e6b9d6e.png)\n\nLet $\\Delta x_i$ be the difference in the $x$-values of any two successive points in $P_1 = \\{x_0, x_1, x_2, x_3\\}\\mathbin{:}$ \n\n$$\n\\Delta x_i = x_i - x_{i-1}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, let $\\Delta y_j$ be the difference in the $y$-values of any two successive points in $P_2= \\{y_0, y_1, y_2\\}\\mathbin{:}$ \n\n$$\n\\Delta y_j = y_j - y_{j-1}\n$$\n\nIt turns out that evaluating double sums over rectangular partitions is important in some parts of higher-level math. For example, how do we compute the sum below?\n\n$$\n\\sum_{i=1}^m\\sum_{j=1}^n \\Delta x_i \\Delta y_j\n$$\n\nFirst, note that we can use the product rule for double summations to write this sum as a product of two separate sums:\n\n$$\n\\sum_{i=1}^m\\sum_{j=1}^n \\Delta x_i \\Delta y_j = \\sum_{i=1}^m \\Delta x_i \\cdot \\sum_{j=1}^n \\Delta y_j\n$$\n\nNow, recall that for partitions of intervals, the sum of differences in successive points is equal to the length of the interval.\n\n- Here, the $x_i$'s partition the interval $[1,4]$ which has length $4 - 1 = 3.$ So, we have $\\displaystyle \\sum_{i=1}^3 \\Delta{x}_i = 3.$\n\n- Similarly, the $y_j$'s partition the interval $[2,4]$ which has length $4 - 2 = 2.$ So, we have $\\displaystyle \\sum_{j=1}^2 \\Delta{y}_j = 2.$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}\\cdot {\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\  & =3\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Note:** There is plenty of geometric intuition here.\n\n- $\\displaystyle \\sum_{i=1}^m \\Delta x_i = 3$ represents the width of the rectangle, while $\\displaystyle \\sum_{j=1}^n \\Delta y_j = 2$ represents the height.\n\n- $\\displaystyle \\sum_{i=1}^m\\sum_{j=1}^n \\Delta x_i \\Delta y_j$ represents the area of the rectangle." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180710 #edb/ref 1065 5798 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180710 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "3e13206a-d7f4-54d7-aa8c-37e9c0e3d26c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186180710 #edb/ref 1067 "Calculating a Double Sum Over a Rectangular Partition" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186254244 #edb/ref 1080 "8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186254244 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186254244 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "43466d22-8b48-55a6-bf28-957026cac2ea" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186254419 #edb/ref 1080 "5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186254419 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186254419 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "55b18526-955c-50d0-b566-01dce50dca98" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186254442 #edb/ref 1080 "20" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186254442 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186254442 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "57c1775a-dfcb-570e-be88-c4c7df1d41a8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186255125 #edb/ref 1080 "10" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186255125 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186255125 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a4e273af-9b7d-518f-9227-01b071590528" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186255282 #edb/ref 1080 "15" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186255282 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186255282 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "b638c667-208e-545f-9953-26e2b3c9f50c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186255963 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186254244 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186255963 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186254419 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186255963 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186254442 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186255963 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186255125 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186255963 #edb/ref 1075 #