m }_{j=1}^{n}3Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j},$ where $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339124 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9f73aa4c-df24-5091-bd74-35aefea94a85" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339124 #edb/ref 1074 "Using the constant multiple and product rules, we can write the summation as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}3Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} & =3{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j} \\\\  & =3{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}$ and ${\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}$ are just the lengths of the intervals $[0,1]$ and $[1,2]$ respectively. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i} & =1-0=1, \\\\ {\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j} & =2-1=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombining our results, we have \n\n$$\n3{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}=3\\cdot 1\\cdot 1=3.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525285 #edb/ref 1080 "25" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525285 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525285 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2288ceae-bccd-555e-852b-d54d20d7465a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525297 #edb/ref 1080 "10" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525297 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525297 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "265ebb5d-6013-56b6-a1e4-0de08d94c7d2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525303 #edb/ref 1080 "-24" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525303 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525303 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "289af18b-9383-5f99-b9af-ddbce979114a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525306 #edb/ref 1080 "6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525306 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525306 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "294c3cc6-d662-53c9-b36e-6a5692b9f4aa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525319 #edb/ref 1080 "2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [175921