 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186525385 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525973 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186525599 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525973 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186525836 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525973 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525973 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525973 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186525341 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525973 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "f33d0ea6-6ed6-5644-82ce-5069ef8f9fbd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525988 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186525889 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525988 #edb/ref 1069 "q-123070" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525988 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525988 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the following partitions:\n\n- ${P}_{1}=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\}$ is a partition of the interval $[1,5]$\n\n- ${P}_{2}=\\{{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}\\}$ is a partition of the interval $[5,7]$\n\nCalculate ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j},$ where $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525988 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "18882139-e768-512f-b798-8450fe515622" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186525988 #edb/ref 1074 "Using the product rule, we can write the summation as\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}.\n$$\n\nNote that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}$ and ${\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}$ are just the lengths of the intervals $[1,5]$ and $[5,7]$ respectively. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i} & =5-1=4, \\\\ {\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j} & =7-5=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombining our results, we have\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}=4\\cdot 2=8.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186526001 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186525884 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186526001 #edb/ref 1069 "q-72482" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186526001 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186526001 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the following partitions:\n\n- ${P}_{1}=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\}$ is a partition of the interval $[1,4]$\n\n- ${P}_{2}=\\{{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}\\}$ is a partition of the interval $[1,5]$\n\nCalculate  ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j},$ where $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186526001 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2eda7c70-df6a-5426-8bab-8b4a22231bc8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186526001 #edb/ref 1074 "Using the product rule, we can write the summation as\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i}\\cdot {\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}.\n$$\n\nNote that ${\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}$ is just the length of the interval $[1,5].$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}=5-1=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the sum over $i,$ we can evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i} & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{0})Δ{x}_{1}+({x}_{2}+{x}_{1})Δ{x}_{2}+⋯+({x}_{m}+{x}_{m-1})Δ{x}_{n} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{0})({x}_{1}-{x}_{0})+({x}_{2}+{x}_{1})({x}_{2}-{x}_{1})+⋯+({x}_{m}+{x}_{m-1})({x}_{m}-{x}_{m-1}) \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2})+({x}_{2}^{2}-{x}_{1}^{2})+⋯+({x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{m-1}^{2}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{x}_{1}^{2}}-{x}_{0}^{2})+(\\cancel{{x}_{2}^{2}}-\\cancel{{x}_{1}^{2}})+⋯+({x}_{m}^{2}-\\cancel{{x}_{m-1}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-{x}_{0}^{2}+{x}_{m}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & ={4}^{2}-{1}^{2} \\\\  & =15\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombining our results, we finally arrive at\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i}\\cdot {\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}=15\\cdot 4=60.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186526042 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186525966 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186526042 #edb/ref 1069 "q-123067" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186526042 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186526042 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the following partitions:\n\n- ${P}_{1}=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\}$ is a partition of the interval $[1,3]$\n\n- ${P}_{2}=\\{{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}\\}$ is a partition of the interval $[3,6]$\n\nCalculate ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j},$ where $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186526042 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "77ce5f28-3326-5c6e-a417-40662b67aeff" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186526042 #edb/ref 1074 "Using the product rule, we can write the summation as\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}.\n$$\n\nNote that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}$ and ${\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}$ are just the lengths of the intervals $[1,3]$ and $[3,6]$ respectively. So, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i} & =3-1=2, \\\\ {\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j} & =6-3=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombining our results, we have\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}=2\\cdot 3=6.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186526047 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186525940 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186526047 #edb/ref 1069 "q-123075" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186526047 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186526047 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the following partitions:\n\n- ${P}_{1}=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\}$ is a partition of the interval $[-3,-1]$\n\n- ${P}_{2}=\\{{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}\\}$ is a partition of the interval $[-2,1]$\n\nCalculate ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}-2({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j},$ where $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186526047 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "84ef10c5-43f7-5edc-8718-6907ea19be0b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186526047 #edb/ref 1074 "Using the constant multiple and product rules, we can write the summation as\n\n$$\n-2{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i}\\cdot {\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}.\n$$\n\nNote that ${\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}$ is just the length of the interval $[-2,1].$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}=1-(-2) & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the sum over $i,$ we evaluate it as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i} & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{0})Δ{x}_{1}+({x}_{2}+{x}_{1})Δ{x}_{2}+⋯+({x}_{m}+{x}_{m-1})Δ{x}_{n} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}\\,+\\,{x}_{0})({x}_{1}\\,-\\,{x}_{0})\\,+\\,({x}_{2}\\,+\\,{x}_{1})({x}_{2}\\,-\\,{x}_{1})\\,+\\,⋯\\,+\\,({x}_{m}\\,+\\,{x}_{m-1})({x}_{m}\\,-\\,{x}_{m-1}) \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2})+({x}_{2}^{2}-{x}_{1}^{2})+⋯+({x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{m-1}^{2}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{x}_{1}^{2}}-{x}_{0}^{2})+(\\cancel{{x}_{2}^{2}}-\\cancel{{x}_{1}^{2}})+⋯+({x}_{m}^{2}-\\cancel{{x}_{m-1}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-{x}_{0}^{2}+{x}_{m}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =(-1)^{2}-(-3)^{2} \\\\  & =-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombining our results, we finally arrive at\n\n$$\n-2{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i}\\cdot {\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}=(-2)\\cdot (-8)\\cdot 3=48.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186526049 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186525973 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186526049 #edb/ref 1069 "q-149632" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186526049 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186526049 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the following partitions:\n\n- ${P}_{1}=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\}$ is a partition of the interval $[1,3]$\n\n- ${P}_{2}=\\{{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}\\}$ is a partition of the interval $[3,5]$\n\nCalculate ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}0.5({y}_{j}+{y}_{j-1})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j},$ where $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186526049 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8659922e-fb1c-5be1-95b0-fc0ad4f5b044" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186526049 #edb/ref 1074 "Using the constant multiple and product rules, we can write the summation as\n\n$$\n0.5{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}\\cdot {\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j}+{y}_{j-1})Δ{y}_{j}.\n$$\n\nNote that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}$ is just the length of the interval $[1,3].$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}=3-1 & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the sum over $j,$ we evaluate it as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j}+{y}_{j-1})Δ{y}_{j} & =({y}_{1}+{y}_{0})Δ{y}_{1}+({y}_{2}+{y}_{1})Δ{y}_{2}+⋯+({y}_{n}+{x}_{n-1})Δ{y}_{n} \\\\  & =({y}_{1}\\,+\\,{y}_{0})({y}_{1}\\,-\\,{y}_{0})\\,+\\,({y}_{2}\\,+\\,{y}_{1})({y}_{2}\\,-\\,{y}_{1})\\,+\\,⋯\\,+\\,({y}_{n}\\,+\\,{y}_{n-1})({y}_{n}\\,-\\,{y}_{n-1}) \\\\  & =({y}_{1}^{2}-{y}_{0}^{2})+({y}_{2}^{2}-{y}_{1}^{2})+⋯+({y}_{n}^{2}-{y}_{n-1}^{2}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{y}_{1}^{2}}-{y}_{0}^{2})+(\\cancel{{y}_{2}^{2}}-\\cancel{{y}_{1}^{2}})+⋯+({y}_{n}^{2}-\\cancel{{y}_{n-1}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-{y}_{0}^{2}+{y}_{n}^{2} \\\\  & ={y}_{n}^{2}-{y}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & ={5}^{2}-{3}^{2} \\\\  & =16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombining our results, we finally arrive at\n\n$$\n0.5{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}\\cdot {\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({y}_{j}+{y}_{j-1})Δ{y}_{j}=0.5\\cdot 2\\cdot 16=16.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
